59	\title{\bfseries Inter-Universal Teichm\"uller Theory\\ in the Paraconsistent Ambient}
60	\author{Lando Mills}
61	\date{}
62	
63	\begin{document}
64	\maketitle
65	
66	\begin{abstract}
67	Inter-Universal Teichm\"uller Theory (IUT) relates two ring structures across
68	the $\Theta$-link by data that is deliberately \emph{not compatible} with either
69	ring structure, and repairs the mismatch only up to three ``relatively mild
70	indeterminacies.'' Read in classical (Boolean) logic, holding two incompatible
71	ring structures together is a contradiction, and a contradiction explodes. This
72	note houses IUT where the incompatibility is not a defect: the four-valued
73	paraconsistent ambient of Belnap FOUR. The central claim is measured, not
74	asserted. The $\Theta$-link word, run through the sixteen-valued Grammar engine,
75	\emph{closes} (control-flow verdict $T$, the composition $\mu\circ\delta=
76	\mathrm{id}$) while its final register is $A=\{T,F,t,f\}$, which projects to the
77	four-valued core as $B$ (both). $B$ is the Inclosure: the paraconsistent closure
78	that the Boolean core's two adjoints, the reflector and the coreflector, cannot
79	recover. So the alien ring structure carried across the $\Theta$-link is the
80	value $B$, held without explosion, and the reason classical mathematics finds IUT
81	unhoused is that the Boolean core has no cell for $B$: it can only collapse the
82	link, erasing exactly its content. The three indeterminacies are the ambient's
83	native $N$ and $B$; conjugate synchronization is the all-lane register syzygy the
84	Grammar already measures. This houses IUT's logical core; it does not reprove the
85	diophantine conclusions.
86	\end{abstract}
87	
88	\section{The paraconsistent ambient}
89	
90	The ambient is Belnap--Dunn FOUR, $\mathbf{4}=\{N,T,F,B\}$: a value may carry
91	neither truth nor falsity ($N$), exactly one ($T$ or $F$), or both ($B$). The two
92	classical values $\mathbf{2}=\{F,T\}$ form the \emph{Boolean core}, a proper
93	substructure. The passage from FOUR to the Boolean core is a semantic
94	restriction, and it is realised by two different universal maps
95	(\texttt{UNO.tex}; \texttt{belnap.rs}):
96	\begin{itemize}
97	\item the \emph{reflector} $r$, the least Boolean value above $v$ in the truth
98	order, with $r(N)=r(B)=T$ and $r(T)=T,\ r(F)=F$;
99	\item the \emph{coreflector} $c$, the greatest Boolean value below $v$, with
100	$c(N)=c(B)=F$ and $c(T)=T,\ c(F)=F$.
101	\end{itemize}
102	The reflector and coreflector erase the same two nonclassical inputs ($N,B$) in
103	opposite directions. Beside them sits the \emph{Inclosure}, the constant
104	paraconsistent closure
105	\[
106	\mathrm{Inc}(v)=B \quad\text{for every } v,
107	\]
108	a fixed point ($\mathrm{Inc}(B)=B$) that lives outside the Boolean core entirely.
109	The decisive fact is that no Boolean endomap recovers it.
110	
111	\begin{theorem}[Corollary 11.2, \texttt{UNO.tex}; checked in \texttt{belnap.rs::corollary\_11\_2\_report}]
112	$r\circ\mathrm{Inc}$ is constant at $T$ and $c\circ\mathrm{Inc}$ is constant at
113	$F$, over all four inputs; neither equals $\mathrm{Inc}(v)=B$. The Boolean core
114	cannot represent $B$.
115	\end{theorem}
116	
117	This is the whole leverage of what follows. A structure whose value is $B$ is
118	visible in the ambient and invisible to the Boolean core, which can only send it
119	up to $T$ or down to $F$ and, either way, lose it.
120	
121	\section{IUT, in brief}
122	
123	IUT fixes initial $\Theta$-data (an elliptic curve $E_F$ over a number field, a
124	prime $\ell\ge 5$, and auxiliary data) and builds $\Theta^{\pm\mathrm{ell}}$NF-Hodge
125	theaters, ``miniature models of conventional scheme theory'' whose two
126	combinatorial dimensions correspond to the additive and multiplicative structures
127	of a number field \cite{iut1}. Two symmetries act: the geometric
128	$\mathbb{F}_\ell^{\rtimes\pm}$-symmetry (additive) and the arithmetic
129	$\mathbb{F}_\ell^{*}$-symmetry (multiplicative). The theaters are glued by the
130	$\Theta$-link, which relates Frobenioid-theoretic portions of one theater to
131	another \emph{in a fashion not compatible with the respective ring/scheme
132	structures}. Relating the ring structures on the two sides is the ``highly
133	nontrivial'' problem, achieved only up to the three indeterminacies, and the
134	object it produces is named an \emph{alien ring structure}. A further tool,
135	\emph{conjugate synchronization}, permutes copies of the local Galois group
136	$G_{\underline v}$ across labels \emph{without} inducing conjugacy
137	indeterminacies, and is what makes the theta evaluation at $\ell$-torsion
138	well-defined.
139	
140	The Grammar has already decomposed IUT structurally: the theory factors into ten
141	join-irreducible atoms, with $\Theta$-link $\equiv$ Log-link at distance $0$ and
142	Anabelian $\equiv$ Frobenioid at distance $0$
143	(\texttt{iutt\_deep\_decomposition}), a primitive-by-primitive translation into
144	conventional language (\texttt{iutt\_clink\_translation}), and a kernel-checked
145	reading of the $\Theta$-link as a twelve-opcode program
146	(\texttt{iutt\_imasm\_verification}). What has been missing is the binding of that
147	decomposition to the paraconsistent ambient. That binding is the housing.
148	
149	\section{The housing}
150	
151	\subsection{The \texorpdfstring{$\Theta$}{Theta}-link is the Inclosure}
152	
153	The IUT ob3ect mints the full-theory word
154	\[
155	\mVinit\mVinit\mVinit\mVinit\,\mFsplit\,\mAfwd\,\mEvalt\,\mClink\,\mImscrib\,
156	\mArev\,\mEvalf\,\mEngagr\,\mClink\,\mFfuse\,\mIfix\,\mTanch,
157	\]
158	and the $\Theta$-link edge is the frobenioid coupling
159	\[
160	\mVinit\,\mImscrib\,\mAfwd\,\mFsplit\,\mEvalt\,\mArev\,\mEvalf\,\mFfuse\,\mClink\,
161	\mEngagr\,\mIfix\,\mTanch .
162	\]
